## What I built

**Builder** — `Environment/Editor/LadyLakeEnvironmentBuilder.cs` (77 KB) with `public static LegacyGwent.LadyLakePremium.Editor.LadyLakeEnvironmentBuilder.Build()` plus a menu item. It produces `Environment/Environment.prefab` + 11 baked Unity mesh assets + 13 materials + 7 byte-identical texture copies + Animator assets + `catalog-fragment.json` + `environment-build.json`.

**Real 3D modelling** (no flat planes, no runtime procedural renderer): a curved backdrop shell, a dune waterbed grid, a bed-caustics overlay, a full-frame caustic sheen, 6 volumetric sun shafts crossing depth, 17 kelp fronds in 3 depth bands, a 7-pad domed lily canopy with stems, 3 depth-separated particle fields, and a crossed-quad sword-glow halo. Everything is authored in the contract frame `P((px-248.5)/100,(355-py)/100,z)` with `k = 1 + z/11.5` perspective compensation, so depth never distorts the composition. Geometry stays at z ≥ 0.30 except the three foreground fronds pinned to the frame edges.

**Original premium asset reuse** — 4 original DynamicCards shaders (unchanged, built-in RP, **no URP, no new shader**), the Aeschna `15010100` Riverbed/Caustics/Shafts/Bubbles/Foliage parameter sets, Seltkirk `20161801` SwordGlow (queue 3021, `_NoiseUV -0.5`, offset `-0.12`), and the original tileable Aeschna textures (GUIDs documented). The selected painting (`background.png`) is copied unchanged and preserved; the waterbed samples its own lakebed band so the modelled bed keeps the painting's palette.

**12 s timing** — Animator `Intro`(12 s)→`Loop`(12 s, loopTime) with integer-cycle sway curves and an `m_Float` curve on the production `DynamicCardAnimatedMaterialProperty`; `LadyLakeEnvironmentCycle` handles the 3.2 s catch glint and 5.6–8.3 s lift swell and rides the rig's real `GripSocket`. Catalog fragment exposes `particleEvents`/`uvMotions`.

**Audio** — `Audio/LadyLakeLoop.wav`: 12.000 s, **stereo** 48 kHz 16-bit, per-channel peak **27570 = −1.50 dBFS, 0 clipped samples**, DC removed, 0.35 s loop crossfade. Derived from 5 original premium scene soundtracks (Aeschna 15010100, DIY-art 56180101, Tempest 16550101, Syanna 13680101, Will of the Wisps 22500101) via a reproducible pure-Python processor. Full provenance + peak + attribution in `audio-provenance.json`; **no speech used**.

**No duplicate audio** — the prefab deliberately contains no `AudioSource`, `AudioListener`, `Camera` or `Light`; production `DynamicCardView` creates the single `AudioSource` from the catalog `audio` field.

